      "text": "VISUAL DIRECTION: Toy Box (Chunky, rounded, celebratory)\nColor strategy: Full palette with darker 'edge' shades for a tactile 3D press\nTypography: Rounded heavy headings at 28–40px, rounded body at 16–17px weight 600–700. Big, friendly, sentence case.\nColor: A bright primary (grass green, tomato, sky) with a darker edge shade for each fill, white surfaces, light gray borders, and dark gray text (not black).\nLayout and composition: Mobile-first single column, 48–56px controls, one big task per screen, character-like shapes.\nComponents: Tactile buttons and cards with a 4px darker bottom border (border-b-4) that disappears on press (translate-y-1); rounded-2xl cards with 2px borders; a chunky progress bar; a bottom tab bar with filled colorful icons.\nImagery: Flat vector characters or toy-like 3D objects.\nMotion: Springy overshoot only for rewards; confetti only on completion.\nSignature moves to choose from: Tactile buttons with a darker bottom edge; A chunky progress bar or XP counter; A celebration state.\nNever: No hairline type; No dark muted palettes; No sharp corners; No dense tables; No bounce on routine navigation.\nThe cliché rendition to avoid: Random rainbow colors with emoji everywhere. Toy Box is one bright primary used consistently."
